{
  "id": "public-keyed-columnar-word-counts",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Source keyword columns at the printed word alignment",
  "question": "What fixed-dictionary word counts follow the source 45 keyword-selected column permutations on original LP2 pages?",
  "reader_question": "Do keyword-selected column orders reveal words at the printed alignment?",
  "summary": "The maximum 126 dictionary hits lies within the 128-trial shuffled full-search baseline: 90 maxima are at least as high. All 45 planted Warning score controls rank the true map first; the post-target comparison remains exploratory.",
  "reader_finding": "The best keyword gives 126 dictionary matches, but shuffled pages commonly score as highly. Known-text tests recover the intended reading. These word matches do not confirm plaintext.",
  "reader_limit": "The shuffled comparison was designed after seeing the result, so it is exploratory. Only these 45 keyword labels, this dictionary and the original visible word lengths were tested.",
  "finding": "Original 45 labels/43 column orders yield 126 maximum hits across 2,776 slots. In 128 post-target shared-page shuffled full 45-label searches, maxima range 116–144 (mean 127.789), with 90 at least 126. The existing 184-rune Warning has 45 known word slots and 30 dictionary hits; all 45 planted-key scoring controls recover exact plaintext and rank the true map first, with only equivalent-key ties. Earlier 1,125 transformation controls remain separate.",
  "outcome": "inconclusive",
  "limitations": "Post-target exploratory null choice cannot establish a prospective significance claim. Score/rank power is checked on one known reading with its available punctuation/hyphen boundaries, while target slots follow the frozen hyphen-only rule. No general-language power or plaintext exclusion is claimed. Original source absolute-path corpora and first 55-block selection were not exact-replayed; its invalid modulo 26 one-long-word control is excluded.",
  "next_steps": "A prospective test should freeze an independent reading/continuation criterion and matched full-selection null before examining a new target observable.",
  "tags": [
    "LP2",
    "source followup",
    "keyed columnar",
    "transposition",
    "dictionary counts"
  ],
